  "limitations": [
    "The coefficient-state lower bound omits temporary arrays, caches, input plans, interpreter/library memory and result objects. It is not a measured process peak.",
    "Default eligibility is only the constructor-level arithmetic. Public calls also charge input plans, retained response caches and pending response batches; eligibility does not promise runtime or learning quality.",
    "All grid methods retain the full Cartesian signed spectrum, including mixed signs. The grid and coefficient-pair guards apply to response methods, not direct adjoint or occurrence shifts.",
    "At p=8,r=1 the response has 6561 grid points and is rejected by the default4096 limit even when memory is otherwise sufficient. This is a configured exact-response boundary, not a statement that eight-parameter circuits cannot run.",
    "n=20 and n=24 examples are unsupported extrapolations beyond the implemented16-qubit cap. They were not executed.",
    "These are classical simulator memory requirements. They do not estimate physical QPU qubits, hardware runtime or a quantum advantage.",
    "A single shared parameter with many occurrences is materially different from many independently trainable parameters. Keeping total gate occurrences fixed does not keep response size fixed."
